    "finding": "All three engines agree exactly at 96, 512 and 1024 ids, and the fp32 top-2 margins are 12.31 to 13.46. The 96-id point is the same length that disagrees under the probe corpus, so length alone does not predict the outcome. This establishes that the tokenizer, the prompt-id path into both engines, and the comparison itself are sound: a harness defect would not spare the confident rows."
