    "finding": "At 96 ids llama.cpp and fp32 each emit 10 distinct tokens of 16 while the MMQ route emits 3, collapsing into 236832 repeated. The route's first token there is identical to llama.cpp's, so a first-token comparison reports agreement. At 16 and 24 ids all three arms degenerate, which makes those lengths a property of the short prompt rather than of the route, so 96 is the only clean case and it is decisive.",
    "correction": "This supersedes the conclusion recorded from first tokens alone in this artifact, that neither arm is systematically wrong. That reading was correct about what it measured and too narrow to generalise from: confident rows still agree across all three engines, so the low-margin account of the flips survives, but a flip that self-reinforces into a loop is a distinct and worse failure than a flip."
  },
